# openOODA Organization

A systems language for AI-assisted work. Effects take capability tokens.
The product path is: typecheck, emit C / direct machine code, execute.

Public portal: https://openOODA.github.io
Proof stays on the private boards (`openOODA/SHIPPED.oot`).

## Product Scope

- Compiler and CLI live in `ooda`. Commands: `check`, `build`, `run`, `test`, `fix`, `patch`, `lsp`.
- Native backends: C99 + runtime/chs_rt.c, direct x86-64 ELF64, direct AArch64 ELF64, standalone WASM.
- Product standard library in `ooda/std/` (pure `.oo` capability-gated modules).
- Editor support in `vscode/` and `tree-sitter/`.

## Repositories

| Repo | Role | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `openOODA.github.io` | Public portal + documentation | Public |
| `registry` | Package registry catalog | Public |
| `ooda` | Sovereign compiler, CLI, runtime | Private |
| `openOODA` | 9 Process and governance boards | Private |
| `qa` | Hostile adversarial test suite | Private |
| `vscode` | Editor extension | Private |
| `tree-sitter` | Tree-sitter grammar | Private |
| `helloworld` | Starter fixtures | Private |
| `brand` | Design assets | Private |

## Build from Checkout

From an `ooda` tree:

```bash
cd ooda
bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo
./bin/ooda run fixtures/hello.oo
```
